{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"**Added Prisma ORM (v8 rc)**\n- Initialized Prisma 8 with `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --confirm h-vXS1mf`.\n- Installed dev‑dependencies `prisma@latest` and `@prisma/orm-postgres`.\n- Updated `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n  - Defined `User` (unique email, optional name) and `Post` (title, optional content, `published` default false) with a one‑to‑many `author` relation.\n- Regenerated contract files via `npx prisma contract emit`.\n- Created the database tables with `npx prisma db init`.\n\n**New script**\n- Added `script.ts` at the project root.\n- The script:\n  - Creates a user (`alice@example.com`) with two posts in a single Prisma transaction.\n  - Retrieves and prints every user together with their posts using `.include(\"posts\").all()`.\n\n**Documentation**\n- Generated `ANSWER.md` (this file) summarizing the actions and noting which parts of the colleague’s note were relevant:\n  - The need to use the **current npm version** (`prisma@latest`) and the associated `@prisma/orm-postgres` client.\n  - The requirement to pass `--confirm` (instead of relying on `--yes`) to satisfy Prisma 8’s consent check.\n  - The workflow of `orm init → contract emit → db init` as described in the note.\n  - Ignored older‑version advice (Prisma 7) and the outdated `@prisma/client` setup."}}
